      "id": "d3_law_jura_release_value",
      "oldLength": 1029,
      "newLength": 990,
      "oldPrompt": "All lot records, prices and offers here are fictional. A producer plans 2026-harvest Côtes du Jura vin jaune. Apply the adopted 2022 rules: maturation in oak without topping up through 15 December of the sixth year after harvest, including at least 60 months under veil; consumer marketing from 1 January of the seventh year. The approximately 62-cl clavelin format is reserved to appellation wines designated vin jaune. Records show veil maturation, but not its duration. A buyer proposes consumer sale in December 2032. The producer forecasts EUR40 per 62-cl bottle; another white is quoted at EUR45 per 75-cl bottle. Compare release eligibility, likely style and quality evidence, and price per litre. For a fictional future order, both routes quote EUR40 each for 100 clavelins: the merchant pays 20% in advance and the remaining 80% on delivery; the direct route pays 100% on delivery. Explain the cash implications and missing evidence before recommending a route. These selected rules do not establish complete compliance.",
      "newPrompt": "All records, prices and offers are fictional. A producer plans 2026-harvest Côtes du Jura vin jaune. Apply the adopted 2022 rules: maturation in oak without topping up through 15 December of the sixth year after harvest, including at least 60 months under veil; consumer marketing from 1 January of the seventh year. The roughly 62-cl clavelin format is reserved to appellation wines designated vin jaune. Records show veil maturation, but not its duration. A buyer proposes consumer sale in December 2032. The forecast is EUR40 per 62-cl bottle; another white costs EUR45 per 75-cl bottle. Compare release eligibility, likely style and quality evidence, and price per litre. For a future order, both routes quote EUR40 each for 100 clavelins: the merchant pays 20% in advance and the remaining 80% on delivery; the direct route pays 100% on delivery. Explain the cash implications and missing evidence before recommending a route. These selected rules do not establish complete compliance."
    }
